/android/app/debug
/android/app/profile
/android/app/release
# .env is intentionally tracked (see .env in the repo) — it's a placeholder with no real secrets,
# committed so `flutter build` doesn't fail on the missing declared asset. Real per-environment
# values, if ever needed, should come from a CI secret overwriting this file at build time, not by
# re-ignoring and hand-editing it locally.
!.env